sequenceDiagram
  %% Source for 16-image-scan-flow.html. Edit this file, then run ./scripts/render-diagrams.py.
  %% Directives: docs in diagrams/README.md (Updating diagrams).
  %% @subtitle One scheduled or manual run of the fail-closed image scanner
  %% @type security: MON
  %% @type cloud: PX
  %% @type external: FEED
  %% @type database: OUT
  actor TRG as Schedule or operator
  participant MON as image-security-monitor<br/>Trivy scanner
  participant PX as Docker socket proxy<br/>read-only
  participant FEED as Vulnerability feeds<br/>Trivy DB · CISA KEV
  participant OUT as Private evidence<br/>reports · metrics · SBOMs

  TRG->>MON: start a scan run
  MON->>MON: acquire the scanner lock
  MON->>PX: inventory running digests
  PX-->>MON: platform digests
  MON->>FEED: download Trivy DB and CISA KEV
  FEED-->>MON: feeds
  alt feeds stale or invalid
    MON--xTRG: operational failure, nonzero exit
  else feeds fresh and valid
    loop each platform digest
      MON->>MON: scan and apply time-limited exceptions
    end
    MON->>OUT: write private reports and textfile metrics
    alt --enforce and an unexcepted KEV or fixable Critical
      MON--xTRG: release gate fails
    else no blocking finding
      MON->>OUT: generate SBOMs and licence evidence
      MON-->>TRG: run complete
    end
  end
